candidates.screen_sketch:
SCREEN C2 (fixed before data; no claim; CONTINUE or STOP).
Rule 1, Data:
- throw-away INCEPTION day(s) designated by the author;
- Stage 1 counts closing windows per cell before any score is read.
Rule 2, Score, groups, arms:
- score: the line #1 score or C1's decision score; groups as in the algorithm; TTC threshold 8 s fixed;
- arms: F-blind; W-blind; BV (blind-but-valid: one blind constant set so the worst context cell is valid); W_ctx (per-group first 300, then freeze; F_ctx until then); linear QR and GBM QR with the same conformal step; NN variant; O; H and HC (conditional hindsight, report-only).
Rule 3, Decision:
- STOP if (i) context-blind W is A1-valid in every closing cell (nothing to fix);
- STOP if (ii) the HC oracle is < 10 % shorter than BV in every R2/R3 cell;
- STOP if (iii) covariates cut pinball loss by < 5 % against the unconditional quantile;
- STOP if (iv) the calibrated closing-cell gap exceeds a production ACC gap (2 m + 1.0 s*v) in < 5 % of closing windows (it never changes driving);
- otherwise CONTINUE.
Rule 4, Sufficiency:
- >= 1,000 closing windows in >= 10 blocks over >= 3 periods per gated cell, or STOP as untestable;
- <= 5 % clipped scores;
- a robustness row with noisy or dropped second-leader data.
Rule 5, Integrity:
- causal features only; synthetic tests of the Mondrian step; run once; log all.
Strongest simple rivals: W_ctx (a calibrated lookup table) and BV.
NN sub-kill: NN not >= 2 % shorter than GBM, so drop the NN.

