- Medical informatics has mature monitor-then-update methods: Davis et al. 2020, J Biomed Inform (https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8627243).
- Patient monitoring has mature alarm delays, intelligent alarm systems and patient-specific limits.
- Aviation has ASTM F3269-21. Its listed components are Input Manager, Safety Monitor, RTA Switch and Recovery Function, plus "safe boundaries and RTA system coverage" (https://store.astm.org/f3269-21.html).
- Automotive regulation stays with frozen software. A draft UN ADS regulation text reportedly excludes "online in-vehicle learning Artificial Intelligence that self modifies system behaviour" (ECE/TRANS/WP.29/GRVA/2026/3, https://unece.org/sites/default/files/2026-01/ECE-TRANS-WP.29-GRVA-2026-03e.pdf) [VERIFY: search snippet only; the PDF was blocked to me].
- UL 4600 SPIs monitor the safety case, not the algorithm's parameters (https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.00578).
- IEC 62304 is a lifecycle-process standard and offers little algorithmic transfer. Its edition 2 publication status is unclear [VERIFY].

